            notes: "The forests of the mountainsides below the tree line, cooler and wetter with every hundred metres up: firs, spruces and larches with stone pines toward the top in the Alps and Siberia, spruce and subalpine fir in the Rockies, birch and deodar in the Himalaya, cloud forest and polylepis in the Andes. Avalanches clear tracks down them that alder and berries fill.",
        ),
